cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these certified Max-Cut incumbents or witnesses, please cite this repository."
title: "Stanford G-set Max-Cut: Proof-Carrying Incumbent Release"
authors:
  - family-names: Grebeshok
    given-names: Aleksandr
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Certified feasible Max-Cut solutions (proof-carrying incumbents) for six canonical
  Stanford G-set instances (G1, G2, G3, G11, G14, G22). Each instance ships with its
  graph, a binary witness partition vector, SHA-256 checksums, and an autonomous
  pure-Python verifier that recomputes the cut value from the graph alone. Includes
  a new claimed incumbent for G22 (cut 13359, +13 over the published 13346 of
  Helmberg & Rendl, 2000). The release certifies feasible lower bounds, not global
  optimality, except for G11 where a bipartite cut of value m proves optimality.
keywords:
  - max-cut
  - combinatorial optimization
  - benchmark
  - Stanford G-set
  - proof-carrying data
  - certified solutions
type: dataset
